---
import type {GetStaticPaths,InferGetStaticPropsType} from 'astro';
import SiteLayout from '../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Byline from '../../../components/Byline.astro';
import FarmMap from '../../../components/FarmMap.astro';
import {getPublishedPieces} from '../../../lib/lab';
import {FARM_SLUG,FARM_PATH,FARM_DESK_PATH,FARM_BLUEPRINT_PATH,FARM_BRIEF_PATH} from '../../../lib/autonomous-farm';
import {farmChapters,farmReferences,observationExample,commandExample} from '../../../lib/farm-blueprint';
import {farmJourney} from '../../../lib/lab-journeys';
import runtimeUrl from '../../../scripts/lab-experience.js?url&no-inline';
import '../../../styles/lab-experience.css';
export const getStaticPaths=(async()=>(await getPublishedPieces()).filter(p=>p.data.slug===FARM_SLUG).map(piece=>({params:{slug:piece.data.slug},props:{piece}}))) satisfies GetStaticPaths;
type Props=InferGetStaticPropsType<typeof getStaticPaths>;
const {piece}=Astro.props;
const groups=[{name:'Farm resources and crops',ids:['architecture','observations','water','nutrients','crops']},{name:'Animals and food',ids:['livestock','welfare','biosecurity','food']},{name:'Agents and physical actions',ids:['coordination','agents','commands','robots','continuity']},{name:'Security and data',ids:['security','sovereignty']},{name:'People and evidence',ids:['people','evaluation','economics']}];
const aliases:Record<string,string>={commands:'timeout receipt duplicate retry MQTT unknown',continuity:'offline power outage backup disconnect',sovereignty:'privacy GDPR region data exit support',food:'milk eggs meat vegetables traceability recall',people:'farmer approval human override'};
---
<SiteLayout title="Autonomous farm: engineering notes | Fidret Lab" description="Find the farm boundary you need: water, crops, animal care, food, cloud agents, physical commands, security, sovereignty and human response." canonical={`https://fidret.com${FARM_BLUEPRINT_PATH}`} variant="lab">
<main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="reference-page shell"><header class="reference-heading"><a class="text-link" href={FARM_PATH} data-story-return data-return-scenes={farmJourney.steps.map(s=>s.key).join(' ')} data-return-labels={farmJourney.steps.map(s=>s.short).join('|')}>Back to the story</a><h1>The engineering behind the farm.</h1><p>Start with a question, then inspect the boundary. This is the full architecture behind the guided morning and the situation library.</p><p>By <Byline authors={piece.data.authors}/> · Researched 4 November 2026</p><nav class="reference-routes" aria-label="Lab reading routes"><a href={FARM_PATH}>Guided story</a><a href={FARM_DESK_PATH}>All 28 situations</a><a href={FARM_BRIEF_PATH} download>Operating brief</a><a href="#research">Research and limits</a></nav><p class="experience-scope">A fictional, AI-assisted architecture exploration. No farm, animal, robot or cloud service is connected. It is not a validated twin, operating prescription or legal/safety assessment.</p></header>
<div class="reference-reading"><aside class="reference-index" data-topic-finder><div class="reference-finder" data-only-enhanced hidden><label for="farm-topic-search">Find a topic</label><div class="reference-search-row"><input id="farm-topic-search" type="search" placeholder="Try offline, water or privacy" autocomplete="off"/><button type="button" data-clear>Clear</button></div><p role="status" aria-atomic="true" data-find-status>{farmChapters.length} topics shown</p></div><nav aria-label="Farm engineering topics">{groups.map(group=><div data-find-group><h2 class="reference-index-group">{group.name}</h2><ol>{farmChapters.filter(c=>group.ids.includes(c.id)).map(c=><li data-find-item data-find-text={`${c.id} ${c.title} ${c.plain} ${aliases[c.id]||''}`}><a href={`#${c.id}`}>{c.title}</a></li>)}</ol></div>)}<h2 class="reference-index-group">Inspect the contracts</h2><ol><li><a href="#contracts">Example event and command</a></li><li><a href="#research">Primary sources and limits</a></li></ol></nav><p data-find-empty hidden>No matching topic. <button type="button" data-clear>Show all topics</button>.</p></aside>
<div class="reference-prose"><FarmMap/>{farmChapters.map(c=><section class="reference-section" id={c.id} aria-labelledby={`chapter-${c.id}`}><h2 id={`chapter-${c.id}`}>{c.title}</h2><p class="reference-plain">{c.plain}</p>{c.paragraphs.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}<details><summary>Rehearse this boundary</summary><ul>{c.checks.map(check=><li>{check}</li>)}</ul><p>Proposed tests for a future implementation. This Lab has not performed these physical/distributed-system rehearsals.</p></details><p class="reference-source-links">Source basis: {c.sources.map((ref,index)=>{const source=farmReferences.find(r=>r.id===ref)!;return <>{index>0?' · ':''}<a href={`#source-${ref}`}>{source.label}</a></>;})}</p><div class="reference-return"><a href={FARM_PATH}>Guided story</a><a href={FARM_DESK_PATH}>Find a situation</a><a href="#main">Topic finder</a></div></section>)}
<section class="reference-section" id="contracts"><h2>Example event and command</h2><p>Illustrative fields with values omitted. These are not executable messages or a production schema. Implementations also need validation, authenticity, retention, bounded cardinality and a reviewed migration contract.</p><h3>An observation envelope</h3><pre><code>{observationExample}</code></pre><h3>A bounded physical command</h3><pre><code>{commandExample}</code></pre><p>The command service and edge enforce these fields. Describing a limit in a prompt does not enforce it. Recovery must account for crashes around physical action.</p></section>
<section class="reference-section" id="research"><h2>Research and limits</h2><p>The architecture and case combinations are Fidret’s original synthesis. Primary sources support individual constraints; they do not validate the combined farm, establish universal thresholds or confirm a Fidret implementation. Living guidance can change. Jurisdiction-specific examples are identified below.</p><p>The model covers selected action gates, not crop growth, chemistry, animal physiology, economics, networking or robot dynamics. Simultaneous incidents can need protection, notification and reconciliation together even when a teaching case has one primary answer. Research and implementation were AI-assisted under Hadi’s direction.</p>{farmReferences.map(r=><section id={`source-${r.id}`}><h3><a href={r.url}>{r.label}</a></h3><p>{r.scope}</p></section>)}<a class="text-link" href={`${FARM_PATH}sources/`}>Sources and publication record</a></section>
</div></div><footer class="reference-ending"><a class="button" href={FARM_PATH} data-story-return data-return-scenes={farmJourney.steps.map(s=>s.key).join(' ')} data-return-labels={farmJourney.steps.map(s=>s.short).join('|')}>Return to the story</a><a class="text-link" href={FARM_BRIEF_PATH} download>Take the operating brief</a></footer></main><script is:inline type="module" src={runtimeUrl}></script>
</SiteLayout>
